  "term": "HDI",
  "definition": "HDI, or heterogeneity diffusion imaging, is a diffusion MRI method that uses one clinical scan to identify and describe differences within a tumor, including its tissue makeup and small-vessel characteristics. It is mainly used in evaluating primary brain tumors.",
